    "logic": {
      "concept": "A pullback joined in the direction of a trend two horizons wide. The long-horizon proxy - 50 bars of the run's own timeframe scaled to an hour - says which side is permitted; the EMA(5)/EMA(17) ribbon says the fast leg leads; a normalised slope of at least 0.1 ATR per bar says it is accelerating rather than drifting; and a pin bar, engulfing or expansion candle says the pullback actually resolved rather than merely paused.",
      "entry": "LONG when the long-horizon proxy is bullish, EMA(5) > EMA(17), the fast slope is >= 0.1 ATR per bar, the bar is a bullish pin / engulfing / expansion, volume >= SMA(20) x 1.0 and ATR/close > 0.0005. SHORT mirrors it with the slope <= -0.1.",
      "exit": "EMA(5) crossing back through EMA(17), or the ATR stop (1.0x) or target (Nonex) - whichever the bar reaches first."
    }
  },
